 "overview": [
  "Alya is a twin-hull motor catamaran built in 2017 and run by Galaxy Cruises, a Galapagos company with a fleet of naturalist and dive boats. Galaxy calls her the jewel of the archipelago and decorated her in sunset colours and sea turquoise.",
  "She takes 16 guests in nine cabins, five on the Main Deck and four on the Upper Deck, each with a double or twin beds, air conditioning, a safe, a hair dryer and eco-friendly bath products. There is a dining room, an indoor bar and lounge, an outdoor lounge, sun loungers and a jacuzzi on deck.",
  "Every route starts and ends at Baltra. The 4-night Northern Route reaches Genovesa, Santiago, Bartolome and Chinese Hat. The 5-night Western Route works the young volcanic coasts of Isabela and Fernandina. The 5-night Southern Route covers North Seymour, South Plaza, Santa Fe, San Cristobal, Espanola and Floreana. Join two back to back for a longer trip."
 ],
 "why": [
  "Sixteen guests, one guide and a twin hull. Galaxy says the catamaran design is more stable than a single-hull yacht, which matters if you are new to small boats.",
  "The routes are short and they link up. Northern plus Southern, or Western plus Northern, gives you 9 nights without repeating an island, and every one starts at Baltra."
 ],
